Lab Material
Lab 12: Trust Establishment with Active Directory
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the concept of cross-domain trust between IdM and Active Directory
Configure and establish trust relationships using the ipa trust-add command
Verify trust status and configure trust settings appropriately
Test and validate cross-domain authentication between IdM and AD environments
Troubleshoot common trust establishment issues
Implement secure cross-domain user access controls
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with Red Hat Identity Management (IdM) concepts
Knowledge of Active Directory fundamentals
Understanding of DNS configuration and Kerberos authentication
Completion of previous IdM labs or equivalent experience
Basic networking concepts including firewall configuration
